data:
After watching reviews I became with an (wrong) idea that this game was similar to civilization games. I was (very) wrong. While it has a few aspects like population and resources management, it also has a lot of what makes Age of Empires cool but in the Norse mythology world. It's clearly a throwback to the golden age of RTS games, the game has great sounds, ambience, Norse mythology lore and a real feel of progress throughout the match. Definitely a must have for any medieval old-school RTS fans.

Pros:
- Norse Mythology done right;
- Great sounds;
- Great Ambience;
- The progress is palpable throughout the match;
- A great diversity of clans that each play very different from one another (As in completely different mechanics, not just little passive boosts)
- Summer and Winter cycles that affects everything from resource management to troops effectiveness;
- Conquest mode (the best mode available with infinite replayability);
- Randomly generated maps in each match;

Cons:
- For beginners resource management could be a bit hard and take away some of your attention from the best parts of the game;
